# Security review

No vulnerabilities found.

The identification sub-task returned NO FINDINGS for the four changed task
scripts, so no false-positive filter ran:

- code/lint/android: the Groovy init script is fixed text; module folders reach
  it only through BOOTSTRAP_LINT_MODULES, split on newlines and used as File
  paths. The eval of usage_files predates the branch and its input is a CLI flag.
- setup/deps/android: file names from `git ls-files -z`, quoted grep arguments.
  A tracked file name that starts with `-` can be read by grep as an option (no
  `--`); worst case is wrong detection, no code execution. SDK level limited to
  digits before `android sdk install`.
- setup/deps/kotlin: fixed init script; mktemp -d with an EXIT trap; file writes
  removed, none added.
- setup/deps/swift: reorders checks and adds a `swift --version` probe; no new
  input handling.
